</div>
<div class="fn" id="doi250014t1n4">
<sup>
<sup>d</sup>
</sup><p class="display-inline">Patients were counted once in the main category of systemic treatments if they received any systemic therapy, and separately, in applicable subcategories (eg, systemic corticosteroids, immunomodulators, biologics) per specific treatments received.</p>
</div>
</div></section><section id="H2-6-DOI250014"><h3 class="pmc_sec_title">Efficacy</h3>
<p>At week 16, an IGA response was reported by 41 of 113 patients in the 4-mg group (36.3%), 47 of 112 in the 8-mg group (42.0%), and 10 of 111 in the placebo group (9.0%) (<a href="#doi250014f2" class="usa-link">Figure 2</a>A); the differences from placebo were 27.5% (95% CI, 17.2-37.8; <em>P</em> &lt; .001) for the 4-mg group and 32.1% (95% CI, 22.1-42.2; <em>P</em> &lt; .001) for the 8-mg group (<a href="#doi250014t2" class="usa-link">Table 2</a>). Similarly, at week 16, an EASI-75 response was reported by 61 of 113 patients in the 4-mg group (54.0%), 74 of 112 in the 8-mg group (66.1%), and 24 of 111 in the placebo group (21.6%) (<a href="#doi250014f2" class="usa-link">Figure 2</a>B); the differences from placebo were 30.5% (95% CI, 18.8-42.1; <em>P</em> &lt; .001) for the 4-mg group and 43.2% (95% CI, 32.6-53.8; <em>P</em> &lt; .001) for the 8-mg group (<a href="#doi250014t2" class="usa-link">Table 2</a>). Subgroup analyses showed that both of the ivarmacitinib groups consistently had greater IGA and EASI-75 responses than placebo across nearly all prespecified subgroups at week 16 (eFigures 2 and 3 in <a href="#note-DOI250014-1-s" class="usa-link">Supplement 3</a>).</p>
<figure class="fig xbox font-sm" id="doi250014f2"><h4 class="obj_head">Figure 2.  Co-primary End Points at Week 16 of Ivarmacitinib Treatment for Moderate to Severe Atopic Dermatitis in Adults and Adolescents.</h4>
<p class="img-box line-height-none margin-x-neg-2 tablet:margin-x-0 text-center"><a class="tileshop" target="_blank" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/core/lw/2.0/html/tileshop_pmc/tileshop_pmc_inline.html?title=Click%20on%20image%20to%20zoom&amp;p=PMC3&amp;id=12044538_jamadermatol-e250982-g002.jpg"><img class="graphic zoom-in" src="https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/5e77/12044538/52b8f7bf1c65/jamadermatol-e250982-g002.jpg" loading="lazy" height="863" width="780" alt="Figure 2. "></a></p>
<div class="p text-right font-secondary"><a href="figure/doi250014f2/" class="usa-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open in a new tab</a></div>
<figcaption><p>A, An IGA response was achieved in 41 of 113 patients (36.3%) in the 4-mg ivarmacitinib group, 47 of 112 patients (42.0%) in the 8-mg group, and 10 of 111 patients (9.0%) in the placebo group. B, An EASI-75 response was achieved in 61 of 113 patients (54%) in the 4-mg group, 74 of 112 patients (66.1%) in the 8-mg group, and 24 of 111 patients (21.6%) in the placebo group. Conclusion of statistical significance was controlled for multiplicity only at week 16. Error bars represent 95% CIs. EASI-75 indicates Eczema Area and Severity Index (75% improvement or greater), and IGA, Investigator Global Assessment (clear [score 0] or almost clear [1] with ≥2-grade improvement).</p>
<p><sup>a</sup><em>P</em> &lt; .001 vs placebo.</p></figcaption></figure><section class="tw xbox font-sm" id="doi250014t2"><h4 class="obj_head">Table 2.  Primary End Point, Key Secondary, and Additional Efficacy End Points at Week 16 of Ivarmacitinib Treatment for Moderate to Severe Atopic Dermatitis in Adults and Adolescents, by Study Group.</h4>
<div class="tbl-box p" tabindex="0"><table class="content" frame="hsides" rules="groups">
<col width="22.28%" span="1">
<col width="23.82%" span="1">
<col width="24.78%" span="1">
<col width="29.12%" span="1">
<thead>
<tr>
<th rowspan="3" valign="top" align="left" scope="col" colspan="1">Measures</th>
<th colspan="3" valign="top" align="left" scope="colgroup" rowspan="1">Study group, No. (%; 95% CI)</th>
